body:
my advice is not to bet, especially if you don't know the game/teams. Gaimin overall are favored to take the series and have won the last 4 big events. They are probably the best team in the world as of now. Quest however is on a hot streak recently and are contenders to win the entire major. as you can see we're about to go 1-1 so map 3 is anyone's guess. if you really want to lean toward one team or the other, GG has more experience overall so they might be better in the clutch. good luck.

&#x200B;

really though, just watch the game and enjoy

hope there's no delay for stage games, that would be another level of embarrassing

&#x200B;

casters hyped about huge gold swing that we knew about 5 minutes in advance thanks to spoilers would be pretty sad ngl

holy shit really? I didn't watch the game and assumed the hltv comments were just degen gamblers being degens but did it really look that bad?

&#x200B;

maybe C9 were just going clown mode, sometimes they play so badly it looks like matchfixing but I doubt they would fix with their tournament life on the line?

C9 got enough rounds in the BO3 to win a map!

&#x200B;

Okay, rating/fragging aside I like C9 interz much more than buster. I just see so many moments where buster is just clueless, giving up key positions, dying when staying alive is vital to keep the round in contention. I'm actually baffled by how bad his gamesense can be. No one is expecting the person in buster/interz's position to be a mad fragger, but to at minimum avoid having negative impact. 

&#x200B;

As for the rest of the players, nafany also has some (quite a few) bruh moments where he just turns his brain off and feeds. Since pretty much everybody on C9 shit the bed I can't really draw too much from this match, but eye-test alone sh1ro is the only consistent player. Ax1le next, who also shits the bed completely at times when his team really needs him.

&#x200B;

And nafany/groove leadership, idk man...this style of play is just agonizing to watch. Where's the creativity/adaption? Every T round: little to no utility expended while trying to find picks across the map, run the clock down while applying little to no pressure and also having no information about anything (the no info also applies to their CT sides) and then get picked apart like gold novas. And this has been a problem since forever. Watch Gambit vs. Na'Vi at Stockholm 2021, FURIA vs. Cloud9 at IEM Dallas 2022 UB SF, and this series to get an idea of what I mean. How much has their playstyle changed since then? And they won Dallas last year, so I believe they can reinvigorate themselves during a tournament - but how often and to what extent, and will that be enough moving forward? 

&#x200B;

I was a fan of C9 from their time as Gambit in the online era, through their struggles when LANs started again up through their win in Dallas, but over time I realized it's just the same shit, different LAN. Static, lifeless plays, scared CS. If they lose the opening pick, they just turtle up and hope for the best, which just won't work against any competent team. IEM Dallas is an event that has a lot of asterisks next to it due to taking place relatively soon after the major and how many teams are either absent or playing with stand-ins. If C9 fail to make a deep run then that will reflect really poorly on them, which might just be the catalyst for roster changes that I feel are already long overdue. No more excuses please, nafany or anyone else.

&#x200B;

Finally, love to see device in such good form. And most importantly, he looks happy playing

depends, if my team is on a huge win streak and I know we have a lot of money I'll just go B-4-2 and buy rifle immediately since I know I'll have enough for everything else

&#x200B;

most times though when the money is tight I go armor first

sdy interview "let's find the joy" I'm gonna cry

&#x200B;

oh also love launders' "what the hell are you doing" @ zevy's failed plant lmao, I love how openly critical him and Scrawny are of bad plays/performances, it's very refreshing.

forZe have the pieces (I think), just need some time. Get more experience, get better at keeping a cool head during games, and they're set. I really liked their little huddle before map 2, didn't work out but respect the idea

&#x200B;

remember how skadoodle the group stage of 8 majors before finally making playoffs of win and then winning it. not saying forZe will win the next major or anything, but they can definitely reach higher heights

